eady exists and is up to date...\" Hmm.\n\nActually, I recall the specific known behavior: **link.exe does NOT regenerate the import library if it already exists and is up-to-date with respect to the DLL's exports.** This is why people often see the error \"LNK1104: cannot open file 'foo.lib'\" when the .lib is locked by a previous linker invocation, even when relinking would skip it.\n\nOK let me also reconsider: maybe I can actually test this in a read-only-ish way? No — running link creates files. Plan mode forbids. \n\nLet me try one more doc search for the LIB reference \"up-to-date\". Let me fetch the LIB reference page. Actually, let me search DDG for \"lib.exe up to date skip overwrite import library\".\n\nLet me do that one search and then finalize the answer regardless.\n\nActually, I think I've spent enough on verification. The answer is solid:\n- Behavior: FACT (evidence).\n- Import lib content = f(exports): FACT (docs).\n- Linker skips rewrite when exports unchanged (content-based check, not timestamp): this is the mechanism explanation. Confidence: reasonable-high given the evidence (lib older than objs but still skipped rules out a timestamp check). I'll mark it honestly.\n\nLet me write the answer in Russian, concise but complete, with confidence markers per the course's anti-sycophancy protocol.\n\nStructure:\n1. Да, интуиция «пересобрал — перезаписал всё» тут не работает, и вот почему.\n2. Что такое import-библиотека и от чего зависит её содержимое.\n3. Механизм: линкер решает по содержимому (списку экспортов), а не по времени. Доказательство: в твоей рабочей папке .lib (21.08) СТАРШЕ объектов (8:47), которые в него вошли, и всё равно не переписан — значит проверка не по таймстемпам.\n4. Ключевой вывод: make и link живут по разным часам. make верит, что после линка .lib стал свежим; link его не трогал. Поэтому расхождение, поэтому вечная пересборка.\n5. Что .exp обновляется — это промежуточный файл текущего прогона.\n6. Confidence markers.\n\nAlso I should note: the fix direction (delete lib before link to force rewrite) forces the content-based skip to never apply, aligning link's output with make's expectations.\n\nKeep it focused on the question \"почему lib не перезаписывается\". Don't re-raise other problems.\n\nLet me also make sure about the claim \"the .lib is byte-identical if exports unchanged\". The import library contains thunks for each exported function, with the function's name/ordinal. If the export set is the same, the .lib would indeed be identical. The linker could compare the computed export list against the existing .lib's records. This is plausible. Mark as explanation with moderate-high confidence.\n\nLet me write the final answer. Since we're in plan mode and this is a \"why\" question, the answer IS the deliverable. I don't need a plan with edits. I'll just answer, and at the end briefly tie back to the fix (which they haven't approved yet).\n\nActually — the user hasn't approved the fix from two turns ago. They asked a follow-up question. So I should answer the question, not push the fix. But I can note the implication.\n\nLet me write concisely.",
