ed to read the current state. Let me read the Makefile again, particularly the pattern rules section.\n\nLet me also reconsider: the user says \"у меня была проблема с тем что игнорируются заголовочники - можно его менять но обновятся только string_utils/geometry, dll, смотря чей это header. а main-ы которые с ним связаны - нет.\"\n\nSo the original bug: change geometry.hpp → geometry objs + dll rebuild, but t1/t3/t4 mains (which include geometry.hpp) do NOT rebuild. That's the classic missing-header-dependency bug. They fixed it by adding header deps to the pattern rule.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtlety. In the earlier version of the Makefile (that I read), the pattern rule for objs was:\n```\n$(BINDIR)/%$(OBJ_EXT): %.cpp | $(CPP_DIRS)\n```\nThis matches ALL objs including common/geometry_cpp.obj and common/geometry_cpp_dll.obj. But there are ALSO explicit rules for those. Actually, GNU make: if there are multiple rules for the same target, make combines their prerequisites. So the explicit rules for geometry_cpp.obj (which list geometry.hpp) AND the pattern rule both apply → prerequisites merge. That's how geometry_cpp.obj picked up geometry.hpp.\n\nFor the mains (t1 main.obj etc.), only the pattern rule applies, and it didn't list headers → mains never rebuilt on header change. That's the bug.\n\nSo the user added headers to the pattern rule prerequisite. Let me see how they did it. The cleanest way in GNU make: add the headers as a variable, or list them explicitly, or use `$(wildcard common/*.hpp common/*.h)`.\n\nLet me read the current Makefile to see the exact current state.\n\nLet me read the relevant lines.",
