r \"не права\"? Partially. Let me frame it as \"ты права про костыльность, но не права про 'просто пересобрать'\". Be honest and direct, not sycophantic.\n\nOne more consideration — the user's phrase \"но если есть такой инструмент то получается не костыль\" — they're saying \"if there's such a tool, then it's not a hack\". I should address this: the existence of a tool doesn't make it non-hacky. -MP IS a hack/band-aid in the sense that it papers over a limitation. It's just the STANDARD, best-available band-aid in the make idiom. The real fix is a different build system (CMake/Ninja dependency handling). So: \"есть инструмент\" ≠ \"не костыль\". Tools can be pragmatic workarounds. And that's fine — engineering is often choosing the right band-aid.\n\nLet me write this. Keep it structured, honest, in Russian, not too long. Since plan mode, no edits — just answer. Maybe at the end remind the plan is still pending (the -MMD -MP etc.), but keep focus on the question.\n\nActually, given the depth of this discussion, the user is clearly trying to fully understand -MP before approving the plan that includes it. Let me make sure my answer equips them to decide.\n\nLet me write the final answer now.",
